---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { APP, ROTAS } from '../../i18n';
---

<Base lingua="en" pagina="privacidade" titulo="Privacy Policy" descricao="Privacy policy for Selah: Enigmas da Bíblia. Anonymous account for the leaderboard, with no name, email, ads or tracking.">
  <article class="documento">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="data">{APP.nome} · Effective {APP.vigencia.en}</p>

    <div class="resumo">
      <p><strong>In short:</strong> Selah does not ask for your name, email, phone number or a password, and it has no ads, tracking or purchases. For the leaderboard and leagues, the app creates an anonymous account by itself and keeps on our server, in Brazil, only what is needed: a random code, the nickname you choose, your character, your points and your level results. Your nickname stays hidden from other players until you decide to show it, and there is no way for players to contact each other. You can delete everything at any time, inside the app.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>{APP.nome} ("Selah" or "the app") is a Bible puzzle game for iPhone and Android, developed and published by <strong>{APP.responsavel}</strong>, based in {APP.cidade.en}, which is the controller of the data described here. This policy explains how the app handles your information, in line with Brazil's General Data Protection Law (LGPD, Law No. 13,709/2018), Brazil's Digital Statute of Children and Adolescents, and the App Store and Google Play rules.</p>

    <h2>2. Data we process</h2>
    <h3>2.1 Anonymous account</h3>
    <p>The first time you open the app with an internet connection, it creates an anonymous account on our server: a random code, with no name, email, phone number or password. The code is stored on your device so the app keeps using the same account. If you uninstall the app or change devices, a new account is created; since there is no email, we cannot recover the previous one.</p>

    <h3>2.2 Player profile</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>the <strong>nickname</strong> you choose or generate in the app (3 to 16 letters, numbers or underscores) and the date of your last change;</li>
      <li>the <strong>character</strong> chosen from a fixed gallery in the app (no photo uploads);</li>
      <li>whether you appear on the leaderboard with your nickname or as "Anonymous player";</li>
      <li>your league, the frame and title you chose, and your stock of extra hints.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.3 Level results and rewards</h3>
    <p>When you finish a level, the app sends the result: whether it was on the trail or the daily challenge, the theme, the level number, the puzzle type, the difficulty, whether you won, the stars, the time, the mistakes, the hints used, and the day and time it ended. The server calculates the points from this. We also keep your group and position in each week's league and the medals, titles, frames and extra hints you earned.</p>

    <h3>2.4 Reports</h3>
    <p>If you report a nickname on the leaderboard, we keep which player was reported, the reported nickname and which account made the report. The reported player is never told who reported them.</p>

    <h3>2.5 Technical data</h3>
    <p>As with any internet access, the servers receive the IP address and technical information about the connection, which the provider records in security and operation logs.</p>

    <h3>2.6 What we do not collect</h3>
    <p>We do not collect your name, email, phone number, date of birth, location, contacts, photos or your device's advertising identifier. Selah uses no third-party analytics, advertising or tracking tools.</p>

    <h2>3. How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>to show the weekly league, daily challenge and overall leaderboards, and to calculate points;</li>
      <li>to build the league groups, close each week and deliver the rewards;</li>
      <li>to prevent cheating: the server checks every result (for example, a plausible minimum time and levels played at the same time). Results that look impossible stay off the leaderboard and may be reviewed by a person on our team, who decides whether they count;</li>
      <li>to moderate nicknames: a reported nickname may be replaced with one generated by the app, and anyone who breaks the rules may be blocked from the leaderboard.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The legal bases are the performance of the service you use when playing with the leaderboard (LGPD, art. 7, V) and our legitimate interest in keeping the leaderboard fair and safe (art. 7, IX). We do not use your data for advertising, we do not build consumer profiles and we do not sell data.</p>

    <h2>4. What other players see</h2>
    <p>On the leaderboard, other players see:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your <strong>nickname</strong>, only if you turn on "Show my nickname on the leaderboard". This option starts <strong>off</strong> for everyone; while it is off, you appear as "Anonymous player";</li>
      <li>your character, your frame and, together with the nickname, your title;</li>
      <li>your weekly and total points and, on the daily challenge, your stars, time and mistakes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>No one sees your account code. Selah has no chat, messages, friend list or any other way for players to contact each other.</p>

    <h2>5. What stays only on your device</h2>
    <p>These stay only on your device and are not sent to the server:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your trail progress: completed levels, stars, Temple pieces, collection cards and achievements;</li>
      <li>your settings: sound, music, vibration, text size, daily reminder and accessibility options;</li>
      <li>game statistics used only to adjust the puzzles' difficulty to your pace.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Without an internet connection, the game works normally: results wait on your device and go up to the leaderboard when the connection returns.</p>

    <h2>6. Game updates</h2>
    <p>When you open the app with an internet connection, it checks Expo's update service (EAS Update), used to distribute Selah, for a new version of the game content (fixes to texts, puzzles or screens). If there is one, it is downloaded and applied the next time the app opens.</p>
    <p>This check sends only technical information: the system (iOS or Android), the app version and a random code generated by the device for this installation, used only to roll out updates gradually. This code is different from the anonymous account code and is not linked to it. The server also receives the connection's IP address.</p>

    <h2>7. Notifications</h2>
    <p>Selah may send at most one reminder per day, and only if you turn this option on in Settings and grant permission. Reminders are created and scheduled on the device itself: no server sends notifications. You can turn them off at any time in the app or in your system settings.</p>

    <h2>8. Permissions</h2>
    <p>The app does not use the camera, microphone, location, contacts, photos or files on your device. It only uses:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>notifications</strong>, for the optional daily reminder;</li>
      <li><strong>vibration</strong>, as feedback to taps (can be turned off in Settings);</li>
      <li><strong>audio</strong>, to play the game's music and sounds while the app is open;</li>
      <li><strong>internet</strong>, for the leaderboard (sections 2 to 4) and to download game updates (section 6).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Who we share it with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell or share data for advertising. We use two service providers, which process the data only to run the app, on our behalf:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Supabase</strong>, which hosts the leaderboard server (anonymous account, profile, results, leagues and reports). The data is stored on servers in Brazil, in the São Paulo region. Supabase is a company headquartered in the United States;</li>
      <li><strong>Expo</strong>, which delivers game updates, with the technical information described in section 6.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Apple and Google, which distribute the app, may process data about downloads and the use of their stores and systems under their own privacy policies (for example, crash reports you agree to send in your device settings). That data is handled by them, not by Selah.</p>
    <p>We may disclose data when required by law or by a court order.</p>

    <h2>10. How long we keep it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Detailed level results:</strong> 90 days. After that, only the points total remains.</li>
      <li><strong>Profile, points total, league and rewards:</strong> while the account exists.</li>
      <li><strong>Accounts unused for 12 months:</strong> deleted automatically, with all the data linked to them.</li>
      <li><strong>Resolved reports and the history of moderation decisions:</strong> 12 months.</li>
      <li><strong>Provider technical logs:</strong> for the period set in the provider's policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>11. How to delete</h2>
    <p>In the app, tap your avatar at the top of the home screen to open the Profile, then tap <strong>Delete account</strong>. This immediately deletes from the server your anonymous account and everything linked to it: nickname, character, points, results, league, rewards and any reports made by you or about you. Your trail progress, which is on your device, stays. See every step at <a href={ROTAS.excluir.en}>Delete account and data</a>.</p>
    <p>If you no longer have the app, write to <a href={`mailto:${APP.email}`}>{APP.email}</a> with your nickname, or simply wait: an unused account is deleted automatically after 12 months.</p>

    <h2>12. Children and teenagers</h2>
    <p>Selah is intended for users aged 13 and over and is not directed at children under 13. To protect the teenagers who play:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>the nickname starts hidden on the leaderboard for everyone, until the person decides to show it;</li>
      <li>nicknames go through a filter that blocks profanity, insults, emails, phone numbers, links, social networks and full names;</li>
      <li>there is no chat, messaging, photos or any contact between players;</li>
      <li>there are no purchases, and rewards are always free, known in advance and never random;</li>
      <li>any player can report a nickname, and moderators can replace it or block anyone who breaks the rules.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We do not ask for age. Parents or guardians can request deletion of a teenager's data by writing to the email in section 15 with the nickname.</p>

    <h2>13. Your rights</h2>
    <p>The LGPD gives you the right to confirm whether we process your data, to access it, correct it, request its deletion or portability, learn who we share it with, and object to processing. In the app you can already change your nickname, choose whether to appear on the leaderboard and delete your account. For other requests, write to <a href={`mailto:${APP.email}`}>{APP.email}</a> with your nickname. You may also file a complaint with Brazil's National Data Protection Authority (ANPD).</p>

    <h2>14. Security</h2>
    <p>Communication between the app and the server is encrypted. In the database, access rules ensure that each player can only read and change their own data, and points are only recorded after the server checks them. Moderators access only what they need, through a password-protected administration account.</p>

    <h2>15. Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions and requests about privacy in Selah: <a href={`mailto:${APP.email}`}>{APP.email}</a>.</p>

    <h2>16. This website</h2>
    <p>This website is static: it uses no cookies, forms, analytics or tracking. The company hosting the site may record technical access data (such as IP address) for security, under its own policy.</p>

    <h2>17. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with an updated effective date.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
